All 10 failures fixed; `pytest -q` now reports **15 passed**. No test files touched, no skip/xfail markers added.

Changes, by module:

- **`src/auth.py`**
  - `has_permission` compares lowercased roles (`src/auth.py:10`), so `"Admin"`/`"ADMIN"` match `"admin"`.
  - `is_admin_or_owner` uses `or` instead of `and` (`src/auth.py:15`) — admin alone or owner alone grants access.

- **`src/inventory.py`**
  - `__init__` no longer uses the shared mutable default and copies `initial` (`src/inventory.py:13-14`) — two inventories no longer share storage.
  - `add` accumulates: `self._stock.get(sku, 0) + qty` (`src/inventory.py:20`).
  - `reserve` raises `OutOfStock` only when `qty > available` (`src/inventory.py:28`), so reserving exactly the available stock succeeds.
  - `release` raises `ValueError` when releasing more than reserved (`src/inventory.py:34-36`).

- **`src/text_utils.py`**
  - `slugify` lowercases input and collapses runs of separators to a single `-` (tracking `last_was_sep` instead of a single `replace("--", "-")`, which left pairs un-collapsed) (`src/text_utils.py:16-23`). Docstring examples still hold.
  - `truncate` slices to `max_len - len(suffix)` before appending the suffix (`src/text_utils.py:33`), so the total length respects `max_len`.

Final verification: `pytest -q` → `15 passed in 0.02s`.
